From da89d7ea6a81d823968a338452a8b5ae8bd7fa6e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 7 Jul 2026 00:06:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: add Qwen3.6-35B-A3B subject-model support (HF + vLLM)

Adds support for Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B (hybrid GatedDeltaNet/attention
MoE, Qwen3.5-family architecture) as a subject model:

- registry: map Qwen3.6-35B-A3B (BF16 + FP8) to their SAE hub repos
- pipeline: resolve num_hidden_layers/hidden_size from nested
  text_config (Qwen3.5/3.6 ForConditionalGeneration configs); new
  --no-thinking flag so the decision token sits at the final-answer
  position for reasoning models
- extractor: optional chat_template_kwargs (e.g. enable_thinking=False)
  and close_think_block guard for templates that ignore it; default
  behavior unchanged for existing models
- HF activation extractor: locate decoder layers and embeddings under
  model.model.language_model for ForConditionalGeneration wrappers
- vllm: bump pinned wheel 0.18.0 -> 0.19.0 (Qwen3.6 requires >= 0.19);
  patches 01-03 verified to apply cleanly against 0.19.0
- new patches/04_support_qwen3_5_models.patch: delegate
  set_aux_hidden_state_layers through the Qwen3_5 ForConditionalGeneration
  wrapper and capture aux hidden states post-layer in Qwen3NextModel for
  parity with HF forward hooks
- tests for the registry entry and prompt building; docs updates

Note: uv.lock still pins vllm 0.18.0 - regenerate with `uv lock` on a
machine with GitHub access (this sandbox cannot fetch release wheels).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0146AuXii3YX8crc998H4Jjn
